  "privacyDialogTitle": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyEffectiveDate": "Effective · 2026-05-07",
  "privacyClose": "Close",
  "privacySec1Heading": "1. Overview",
  "privacySec1Body": "Termex is an open-source SSH client. We take your privacy seriously: this app does not collect, transmit, or store any user data on Termex servers — Termex has no backend servers.",
  "privacySec2Heading": "2. Data Storage",
  "privacySec2Body": "All data is stored only on your device:\n· Server configs: local SQLite, SQLCipher AES-256 encryption.\n· SSH passwords / key passphrases: system Keychain (macOS) / Credential Manager (Windows) / Secret Service (Linux).\n· AI API keys: same — stored in the system Keychain.\n· Session recordings: local filesystem.\n· Monitor history: local SQLite, SQLCipher encrypted.",
  "privacySec3Heading": "3. Network Connections",
  "privacySec3Body": "Termex only establishes these network connections:\n· SSH connections: direct to the server you specify; no intermediate nodes.\n· AI requests: direct to the AI provider you configure (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.); Termex never acts as a proxy or relay.\n· App updates: queries the official appcast feed for version information.",
  "privacySec4Heading": "4. Team Sync (Optional)",
  "privacySec4Body": "If you enable team features, Termex syncs encrypted configs via the Git repository you specify. Termex is not a sync server; all data is encrypted with the team key before transmission.",
  "privacySec5Heading": "5. Your Rights (GDPR / CCPA)",
  "privacySec5Body": "Because Termex collects no personal data:\n· Data access / export: all data is locally readable.\n· Data deletion: Settings → Privacy → Erase all data.\n· Data portability: Settings → Data → Export encrypted backup.",
  "privacySec6Heading": "6. Contact",
  "privacySec6Body": "The full privacy policy lives at docs/privacy-policy.md in the project repository. For privacy-related questions please contact us via GitHub Issues.",
